  "title": "The article and the cases",
  "note": "Greek nouns change their endings for case: nominative for the subject, genitive for 'of' or 'from', dative for 'to', 'for' or 'with', accusative for the direct object, vocative for calling. The article ὁ ἡ τό (the) shows a noun's gender, number and case. Greek has no word for 'a': λόγος alone means 'a word', ὁ λόγος 'the word'.",
